title: Component Catalog
intro: A second way to add components: browse them all, read what each one does, and see what it needs.
project: Arcade | Catalog Tour
scene: Game

chapter: Two ways to add | The Inspector's Catalog button
create: Sprite
rename: Guard
say: Here's a new sprite in the Arcade template. Let's turn it into an enemy, the way someone new to Griff would.
explain: catalog:button | Catalog | Add Component is still the quick list, for when you know what you want. The new Catalog button is for when you don't.
catalog
explain: catalog:list | Every component | The catalog lists every component, grouped by what it's for: rendering, physics, movement, combat and more. Each says in a line what it does, and which components it needs.

chapter: Reading a component | Documentation and dependencies
browse: Patrol
explain: catalog:docs | What it does | Searching finds Patrol. Its page says what it does in plain words, from the engine's own documentation.
explain: catalog:requires | Requires | And here's what it needs. A patrol only works with a body and a collider on the same entity. The guard has neither, so both are marked to be added. Any kind of collider will do, so it picks a box.
explain: catalog:workswith | Works well with | It also suggests what goes well with it, without needing it. Add a chase, and it patrols until it spots its target.
explain: catalog:properties | Properties | Further down, every property is explained, with the kind of value it takes and what it starts at.
click: catalog:link:Body
explain: catalog:neededby | Needed by | Component names are links. This is Body's page, and it shows the other side: everything that needs a body to work.

chapter: Adding it with what it needs | One click, one undo
browse: Patrol
explain: catalog:plan | What Add does | Before you add anything, it spells out exactly what will happen.
click: catalog:add
explain: panel:Inspector | Added together | The guard now has a box collider, a body and a patrol. That's everything it needs, added in the right order.
key: Ctrl+Z
say: It's one undo step, so a single undo takes all three back off.
key: Ctrl+Y
say: And redo puts them back.

chapter: Scripts too | Documented from their comments
select: Player
catalog
browse: Ship
explain: catalog:docs | A script | Scripts are in the catalog too. The ship's description comes straight from the comment above its class.
explain: catalog:requires | Its requirements | A script declares what it needs with a Requires attribute. The player already has a body and health, so both are ticked.
say: So whether a component comes with Griff or from your own scripts, the catalog shows what it does and what it needs before you add it.
click: catalog:close
